
# Atlas Industrial Supply

A functional front-end for an industrial equipment marketplace. Built for global B2B procurement of heavy machinery components, power transmission parts, and automation gear.

![Atlas Industrial Preview](https://images.pexels.com/photos/162553/keys-workshop-mechanic-tools-162553.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200&h=600&fit=crop)

## What This Is

Atlas Industrial Supply is a marketplace UI prototype aimed at engineers, procurement officers, and maintenance teams. The design stays away from generic SaaS templates and leans into a factory floor aesthetic. Steel grays, industrial blue accents, and caution yellow highlights.

No frameworks. No build tools. Three files. That is it.

## Features

- Product catalog with live filters (category and certification)
- Featured products section with horizontal scroll on mobile
- Category grid for browsing by industrial sector (hydraulics, electrical, pneumatics, power transmission)
- Animated counter stats (countries shipped, dispatch rate, products in stock)
- Sticky navigation bar that gains a shadow on scroll
- Scroll reveal animations on cards and sections
- Responsive layout that works from phone to widescreen monitor
- Clean, readable code with comments where it matters

## Tech Stack

Plain vanilla everything.

- HTML5
- CSS3 (custom properties, grid, flexbox, transitions)
- Vanilla JavaScript (Intersection Observer API, requestAnimationFrame)
- Font Awesome 6 via CDN for icons
- Google Fonts (Inter and JetBrains Mono)

No React. No Tailwind. No npm install. No node_modules black hole.

