That is the whole thing. Three working files.

## How to Run

1. Clone the repository.
2. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.
3. No server needed. No build step. No configuration.

```
git clone https://github.com/Muhammadalimurtadho/atlas-industrial.git
cd atlas-industrial-marketplace
open index.html
```

## Design Decisions

Some notes on why things are the way they are.

**Font choices.** Inter handles dense product data well. JetBrains Mono on SKU codes gives a subtle technical feel without overdoing it. No generic Poppins or Roboto.

**Color palette.** Steel grays dominate because this is industrial procurement. Blue accents for interactive elements. Yellow reserved for high-priority actions like add-to-cart and stat highlights. No purple-to-blue gradients anywhere.

**Layout.** The catalog hero puts filters and products side by side. Users searching for specific parts do not need a motivational headline. They need to narrow down results fast.

**No emoji.** Anywhere. Icons come from Font Awesome. Emoji do not belong on a B2B industrial interface.

**Language.** Written like a human. Short sentences mixed with longer ones. No "elevate your procurement journey" nonsense.

## Browser Support

Tested on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge. Works on iOS Safari and Android Chrome. Intersection Observer has near-universal support since 2019.

